Part 3: Dashboard & Reporting Plan (Portfolio Piece) 
3.1 Dashboard Design and Objectives
Really Big Bank (RBB) developed two Power BI dashboard views to transform the validated financial data from Part 2 into meaningful market intelligence for financially literate, non-technical management. The dashboards address market performance over 90 calendar days, macroeconomic conditions and potential market risks requiring attention.
The dashboards use curated/curated_market_data.csv, containing 86 aligned observations of S&P/ASX 200 closing prices, RBA Interbank Overnight Cash Rates and three calculated financial metrics. Power BI was selected for its interactive visualizations, dynamic reporting and accessibility for management decision-making.
3.2 Market Trends and Macroeconomic Analysis
The primary dashboard displays ASX 200 closing prices alongside the 10-day moving average, allowing management to distinguish daily fluctuations from recent market trends. Four KPI cards summarize the latest index closing price, moving average, cash rate and 14-day volatility.
A macroeconomic comparison presents RBA cash-rate movements alongside ASX 200 performance using separate axes. This enables management to examine potential alignment or divergence between monetary conditions and equity-market movements without assuming causation.
3.3 Risk Monitoring and Management Overview
A Red/Amber/Green (RAG) monitoring indicator was developed using the validated 14-day volatility metric. Volatility below 0.50% is classified as Green, 0.50% to below 0.70% Amber, and 0.70% or above Red. These exploratory thresholds support consistent monitoring but are not formal banking risk limits.
The latest observation triggers a Red signal, indicating elevated volatility under the defined criteria. Dashboard 1 combines these indicators with concise management insights to support interpretation of market conditions.

